---
import Doc from "../layouts/Doc.astro";
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL, SECURITY_EMAIL, REPO_URL } from "../lib/site";
---
<Doc title="Support" description="How to get help with AuditKit: email, GitHub issues, security disclosure, and what to include in a report." lede="Two channels: email for account and billing, GitHub issues for bugs and feature requests. Both are read by the people who wrote the code.">
  <h2>Email</h2>
  <p><a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a> for accounts, billing, plan changes while Stripe is not yet enabled, and anything private. Include your project id (shown on the project overview). Business plans get priority. <code>[OWNER: confirm priority for Business and a response-time commitment]</code></p>
  <h2>GitHub issues</h2>
  <p><a href={REPO_URL + "/issues"} rel="noopener">{REPO_URL}/issues</a> for bugs in the server, SDKs, verifier or this site. Useful: the request id or event id, the verifier's <code>--json</code> output, and which SDK version. Do not post API keys or payloads.</p>
  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>Vulnerabilities go to <a href={`mailto:${SECURITY_EMAIL}`}>{SECURITY_EMAIL}</a>, not to public issues. See the <a href="/security">security page</a>.</p>
  <h2>Status</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/anchors">anchors page</a> is live from the service and shows whether anchoring is running. <code>[OWNER: status page URL once one exists]</code></p>
</Doc>
